tlstunnel
Usage: tlstunnel - HOST PORT

Open a TLS connection to HOST:PORT and pipe stdin/stdout through it.
The literal - means "use stdin/stdout".

	printf 'HEAD / HTTP/1.0\r\nHost: example.org\r\n\r\n' \
	    | tlstunnel - example.org 443

Trust is not read from a directory at runtime: the certificate
authorities in trust/ are compiled into the binary, so the trusted set
is covered by the hash tree and the image signature. A normal system
trusts around 150 roots, any one of which can issue for any name. This
trusts one. A certificate outside that set is refused, not warned about.

See also: nc, wget
